{
  "id": "29449_meikoku",
  "headword": "銘刻",
  "reading": "めいこく",
  "romaji": "meikoku",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "inscription; engraving",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "inscription; engraving; engraved characters",
      "explanation": "Letters or designs carved into metal, stone, or other hard material, or the act of carving them. Also used figuratively for something engraved deeply in the heart or memory."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29449_meikoku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{石碑|せきひ}に{銘刻|めいこく}する。",
      "english": "to inscribe a stone monument.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29449_meikoku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{古|ふる}い{鐘|かね}に{銘刻|めいこく}された{文字|もじ}を{読|よ}む。",
      "english": "to read the characters engraved on an old bell.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29449_meikoku_ex3",
      "japanese": "その{言葉|ことば}は{今|いま}も{心|こころ}に{銘刻|めいこく}されている。",
      "english": "Those words are engraved in my heart even now.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A formal word used both literally for carved inscriptions and figuratively for vivid, lasting impressions.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {石|いし}に{銘刻|めいこく}する: to engrave in stone\n- {心|こころ}に{銘刻|めいこく}する: to engrave in one's heart\n- {銘刻|めいこく}された{文字|もじ}: engraved characters\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {刻印|こくいん}: stamp; engraved mark — emphasizes a stamped or imprinted mark\n- {銘記|めいき}: to bear firmly in mind — figurative only, never a physical carving",
